==English==
===Etymology===
Named for [[w:Siméon Denis Poisson|Siméon Denis Poisson]] (1781-1840), French mathematician.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
'''Poisson's [[ratio]]'''
#Of a [[material]] in [[tension]] or [[compression]], the ratio of the [[strain]] in the direction of the applied [[load]] to the strain [[normal]] to the load.  Abbreviated [[ν]].

====Translations====
*Finnish: [[Poissonin suhde]]
*Italian: [[modulo di Poisson]]

